    "building_only_observations": [
      "2022, 2024 and 2026 imagery releases show the round green central crown, a square stepped central mass, and a smaller curved feature on the river side. Their apparent alignment shifts between acquisitions.",
      "Across-river winter 2011 photo reveals secondary rounded volumes below a stepped cornice; 2016 oblique view shows dark pointed arch openings below separate green copper crown lobes; both depict the square detached belfry independently.",
      "Photographs record down-the-driveway a tall glazed pointed frame directly above a recessed pointed door, with sculptural figures at the sides. The three-slit belfry, its cornice and pyramidal cap belong to the separate bell tower.",
      "The parish records fourteen pointed arches around the round upper storey, 239 sq m of church, a 10 m high roof and three narrowing levels clad in copper. The 357 sq m geodata outline and 21.85 m city extrusion cannot supply the main chapel dimensions."
    ],
    "references_not_used": [
      "2017 and 2013 interior views document the ceiling, neither is substituted for an exterior photograph.",
      "ESRI current imagery zoom 20 returned a grey map-data-not-yet-available tile. Only the real imagery at zoom 19 is used."
    ]
  },
